    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-10-23T09:20:16+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-23T09:20:16+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-22T22:50:16Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-22T22:50:16Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A trough of low pressure lies near the NT border. A slow moving high pressure system in the Tasman Sea maintains a ridge across eastern parts of the state. A trough of low pressure over the far west is forecast to slowly move eastwards on Friday. Another trough and multiple cold fronts move over the state over the weekend. A ridge of high pressure moves into the west on Monday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW009" description="Flinders" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-10-23T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-24T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-22T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-23T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower near the coast in the late morning and afternoon. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. Winds northwesterly 15 to 20 km/h tending northwest to southwesterly in the late afternoon then tending southeast to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h in the evening. Daytime maximum temperatures around 30.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">Moderate</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:20am to 4:40pm, UV Index predicted to reach 9 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-10-24T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-25T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-23T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-24T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Becoming cloudy. Very high chance of showers near the coast, high chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm, possibly severe with damaging winds and large hail south of Hawker from the late morning. Winds northeast to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending north to northwesterly in the middle of the day then tending southeast to southwesterly in the late evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 13 and 19 with daytime temperatures reaching 30 to 35.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-10-25T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-26T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-24T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-25T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Very high chance of showers, most likely in the morning and afternoon. The chance of a thunderstorm in the morning. Winds south to southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 11 and 16 with daytime temperatures reaching between 16 and 21.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-10-26T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-27T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-25T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-26T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Slight chance of a shower near the coast, near zero chance elsewhere. Winds south to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h tending west to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h during the morning then tending south to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 3 and 8 with daytime temperatures reaching between 17 and 21.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
